    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0762" n="650" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg650"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 211.65 C 38.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Chargé to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Italian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Manchester,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-06-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Thanking you for your telegram of yesterday, I have the honor to inform you that
                    the document I requested by my telegram of 23d instant was the preliminary
                    warrant contemplated by article 2 of convention, April, 1884.</p>
                <p>I am not able to answer second part of your telegram, not having yet received
                    instructions, but have ground to believe that Italian Government would be
                    willing to send all documents referring to the case should United States
                    Government wish to have culprit judged by American courts for the crime he
                    committed in Italy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Montagliari.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
